      "pot": {
        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    # Define the daily returns in percentage points\n    returns = [1.5, -0.5, 3.2, -2.0, 0.8]\n\n    # Calculate excess kurtosis using the provided population-moment formula\n    n = len(returns)\n    mean = sum(returns) / n\n    m2 = sum((x - mean) ** 2 for x in returns) / n\n    m4 = sum((x - mean) ** 4 for x in returns) / n\n    excess_kurtosis = (m4 / (m2 ** 2)) - 3\n\n    # Return the answer to two decimal places\n    return round(excess_kurtosis, 2)\n```",
